---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Operating systems, built to be reached"
  description="December Reach develops operating systems and a JavaScript-based, server-side emulation environment that brings real OS source into the web."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Independent operating system development</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Systems built to be <em>reached.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        December Reach develops operating systems and the technology that makes
        their real source accessible through the web. Source is acquired and
        preloaded by the site; emulation runs in a JavaScript backend.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/DecemberReach/reach-to-be-reached" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          Explore OS source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/emulation/">How emulation works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pipeline" aria-label="Source acquisition, backend emulation, and web session pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-head">
        <span>DECEMBER REACH / EXECUTION MODEL</span>
        <span class="pipeline-status">SYSTEM DESIGN</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-steps">
        <div class="pipeline-step">
          <span class="step-number">01</span>
          <div class="step-copy">
            <strong>OS source</strong>
            <small>Load and preload the real project source</small>
          </div>
          <span class="step-tag">ACQUISITION</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">
          <span class="step-number">02</span>
          <div class="step-copy">
            <strong>JavaScript backend</strong>
            <small>Emulation and execution happen server-side</small>
          </div>
          <span class="step-tag">EXECUTION</span>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">
          <span class="step-number">03</span>
          <div class="step-copy">
            <strong>Web OS session</strong>
            <small>Reach the running system through the web</small>
          </div>
          <span class="step-tag">ACCESS</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-foot">
        <span>FRONTEND: SOURCE ACQUISITION</span>
        <span>BACKEND: EMULATION</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="systems" aria-labelledby="systems-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">01 / OS LINEUP</p>
        <h2 id="systems-title">Different systems. Shared ambition.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        December Reach is the OS development side of the ecosystem. Its projects
        target different computing environments while keeping their own identity.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="system-grid">
      <article class="system-card dark">
        <div class="system-card-top">
          <span class="card-index">SYSTEM / 001</span>
          <span class="card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▣</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>auroraADE</h3>
          <p>Aesthetic Desktop Environment. The current target architecture is x86_64.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-bottom"><span>Desktop environment</span><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </article>

      <article class="system-card blue">
        <div class="system-card-top">
          <span class="card-index">SYSTEM / 002</span>
          <span class="card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>haloDOT</h3>
          <p>An operating-system project in the December Reach lineup.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-bottom"><span>OS project</span><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </article>

      <article class="system-card">
        <div class="system-card-top">
          <span class="card-index">SYSTEM / 003</span>
          <span class="card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▤</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>stellaOS</h3>
          <p>A television operating system in the reachOS lineup.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-bottom"><span>TV operating system</span><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">02 / PLATFORM</p>
        <h2 id="architecture-title">The hardware layer matters.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Fabric Dessert defines the virtual board and hardware-facing contracts
        used by the reachOS platform. It is designed to stay separate from the
        browser host.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="data-grid">
      <div class="data-cell">
        <span class="mono">CPU BOUNDARY</span>
        <strong>FRT64</strong>
        <p>Architecture integration boundary for ARM and x86, 32-bit and 64-bit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <span class="mono">MEMORY</span>
        <strong>64-bit address space</strong>
        <p>BigInt-backed physical addressing with sparse memory regions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <span class="mono">DEVICE BUS</span>
        <strong>MMIO / IRQ</strong>
        <p>Device windows, alignment, interrupt lines and enumeration.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <span class="mono">DISPLAY</span>
        <strong>1080 × 2424</strong>
        <p>RGBA8888 framebuffer with a deterministic host-canvas bridge.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/architecture/">Read platform architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/devices/">Device availability <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="split-feature">
      <div class="feature-panel feature-panel-dark">
        <span class="feature-kicker">THE SOURCE</span>
        <h3 id="work-title">Built from real OS code.</h3>
        <p>
          The source repository is the home of the operating-system work.
          The website is its web-facing entry point, not a visual imitation of
          an operating system.
        </p>
        <a class="feature-link" href="https://github.com/DecemberReach/reach-to-be-reached" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          Open reach-to-be-reached <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-panel">
        <span class="feature-kicker">THE EXECUTION MODEL</span>
        <h3>Browser access. Backend execution.</h3>
        <p>
          The frontend acquires and preloads OS source. The JavaScript backend
          handles the emulation. The browser is the access surface, not the
          guest machine's CPU or memory runtime.
        </p>
        <a class="feature-link" href="/emulation/">
          Explore the emulation model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
